{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 133, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling on the direct input-output edge with identity restores a clean residual path, giving large gains (exp 9)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "With a residual already on edge 3, an extra identity into the output reduces effective capacity and was strongly negative (exps 82, 86, 88)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When no direct residual exists, a skip on edge 5 provides a needed shortcut path (exps 83, 87, 90)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the identity link between intermediate nodes in favor of pooling is very harmful (exp 42)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the main input-output residual hurts more than deleting a conv on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the node1-output identity with a conv removes a shortcut and hurts strongly (exps 63, 64)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 3 is only an identity, cutting edge 0 starves the conv branches feeding the output (exps 25-27)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding an identity where no connection existed adds a path without removing a learnable op (exp 80)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacin